      "source": "question",
      "header": "Run lock",
      "question": "Which lock design for running tasks in parallel? Today one lock file per run (runs/<repo>/<run>/lock) is held for the whole run. Tasks of one run already run together (up to concurrency 4) and separate runs already have separate locks. What is actually serial is `factory run --all`, which drives runs one after another, and the max_workers cap, which no code reads.",
      "day": "2026-11-24",
      "theme": "other",
      "outcome": "followed",
      "answer": "D: keep the lock, fix the two real limits (Recommended)",
      "category": "spec and design",
